  "body": "Currently the TransformStream implementation is heavily centred in the TransformStream object. It would be better to encapsulate responsibilities better. We also need to move code and data that is specific to the stream type out of TransformStream.\r\n\r\nDesirable features:\r\n- Allocation of responsibility is \"logical\"\r\n- Inter-object references are minimised\r\n- Resembles the design of ReadableStream and WritableStream\r\n- New types (ie. WritableStream \"byte\" type) can be added without doubling the amount of code\r\n- Minimise amount of polymorphic dispatch\r\n- Minimise code duplication between byte / non-byte versions\r\n\r\nRestrictions\r\n- TransformStreamDefaultController methods must delegate to abstract operations for use by other specifications.\r\n\r\nOddities\r\n- There is one type dedicated to the writable side (TransformStreamDefaultSink) but two dedicated to the readable size (TSDefaultController and TSDefaultSource). Symmetry with Readable and WritableStream implies we should put the type-specific logic in TSDefaultController but symmetry with TSDefaultSink implies that it belongs in TSDefaultSource instead.",
